Package: graphgenerator
Version: @VERSION@
Section: science
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Moisés Maia Neto <moimaian@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), python3-pip
Recommends: python3-pyside6, python3-numpy, python3-pandas, python3-matplotlib, python3-seaborn, python3-openpyxl
Homepage: https://github.com/moimaian
Description: Generate charts (1D/2D/3D) from CSV/XLSX data
 GraphGenerator turns a CSV or XLSX table into a chart: bar, line, scatter,
 stacked/overlapped area, box, violin, histogram, density, heatmap and
 numeric 2D/3D scatter, with trendlines, legends, color palettes and
 export to PNG/JPG/TIFF/PDF/EPS/SVG at a chosen DPI.
 .
 The program is written in Python + PySide6 (Qt). This package installs the
 application in /usr/share/graphgenerator, creates the Menu and Desktop
 shortcut and, if necessary, installs its Python dependencies (PySide6,
 numpy, pandas, matplotlib, seaborn, openpyxl) via pip.
